  "id": "sorting-test",
  "term": "sorting test",
  "definition": "A sorting test is a neurobehavioral assessment in which a person works through a set of cards or card-like images, and performance is scored from response patterns such as errors, repeated responding, and categories completed. It is used to measure executive function, including mental flexibility, and can help detect impairment related to brain disorder or damage.",
